      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "An LZ4-encoded buffer is a sequence of blocks, each beginning with a header.",
      "contextAfter": "A compressed block header consists of the octets `0x62`, `0x76`, `0x34`, and `0x31`. Following that is the size (in bytes) of the decoded (plaintext) data the block represents, and the size (in bytes) of the encoded data stored in the block. The header stores both sizes as (potentially unaligned) 32-bit little-endian values. The actual LZ4-encoded data stream immediately follows the compressed block header.",
